            <ArticleTitle>Gastrohepatic ligament fibrosis following esophageal sclerotherapy: CT findings.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>136-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a case in which CT demonstrated a nonenhancing mass within the gastrohepatic ligament following sclerotherapy of esophageal varices. At surgery this findings was demonstrated to represent multiple thrombosed veins and varices with surrounding fibrosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
